pulation  india's mortality rate ended up being  among the lowest in the world  everyone around could see people  affected by the coronavirus  even if they went to hospital they would  get out of hospital relatively soon and  relatively healthy and here we are even  talking about people aged 70 plus 75  80 and older yeah i mean there was a lot  of theories whether  india reached the level of herd immunity  to that point there were other  theories going around like india's a  warm country whether  you know south asian populations were  more genetically  immune or disposed to not feel the worst  effects of covid  but none of them were particularly well  proven  but the official numbers were kind of  showing that there was something going  on anyway  you saw modi at the world economic forum  saying that india had basically  contained the virus and had saved the  world from corona the central bank  itself the reserve bank of india  came out with a really quite  jubilant statement in january saying  that the country had bent  the virus curve like beckham which was  you know obviously a very odd statement  come out for a central bank  but that was the kind of atmosphere at  the time  you had cinemas opening you had you know  the wedding season started and you had  these  mass weddings these huge beautiful  indian weddings with you know hundreds  and hundreds of people  and all of this was done without that  very clear public health  messaging that you need when you're in  the middle of a pandemic it was almost  like  india was an exceptional country that  didn't succumb  to a pandemic that was affecting the  rest of the world  what became clear very quickly was what  we had suspected all along and what many  epidemiologists had been telling us  which is that india had been severely  under counting both its infections  and its deaths we know that many many  many deaths in normal times in  india aren't properly recorded  particularly when you get into the  hinterland which 