llion doses of its vaccine for the  world and  400 million of those were meant to be  produced by the end of the year now that  didn't really play out as things went  ahead  by january it transpired that only 70  million of those doses had been produced  so far  and in the start of january there wasn't  a huge amount of demand in india because  basically there weren't that many cases  and all the while india's government was  sending tens of millions of doses  out overseas it was engaged in code  vaccine diplomacy it was really trying  to sort of  needle china which was attempting to do  the same at the time as well  india has exported or donated more than  60 million doses of coronavirus vaccines  to countries far poorer than india  it was seen as a massive diplomatic  victory  for india's ruling party little did they  know that  a more potent strain of the virus was at  the same time growing within the people  in india  [Music]  so there were various consequences of  india emerging relatively  unscathed from the first wave one of  those  was the sense to be self-sufficient  [Music]  local manufacturing local  market  [Music]  imposed massive taxes on imported goods  unfortunately some of these goods that  were imported  was stuff that's essential for our  scientist labs to test the virus  the second mistake that was made was the  calling for elections  and not just elections but massive  public rallies  some of them led by prime minister modi  himself  the next round of mistakes that were  made was giving the green light  for massive religious ceremonies a sure  short recipe for a super spreader  the next problem that local authorities  point out is  over centralization of powers within the  prime minister's office  including how oxygen will be shared  between the states  this really has proved to be a game  changer because every time a state fell  short of oxygen it  lacked the powers to go out and get it  for themselves  [Music]  one of the scariest things when 